diff --git a/RELEASE_2.12.0.md b/RELEASE_2.12.0.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..55c9005
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RELEASE_2.12.0.md
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# MSE 2.12.0 Release Notes
+
+**Release Date:** 2026-11-18  
+**Codename:** Universal Question Constructor & Multi-Control Engine (Layer 1)  
+**Target:** Moodle Quiz Assistant (Stay Userscript + Router / Bot Gateway)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+MSE 2.12.0 brings complete, end-to-end support for question types across all 18 Layer 1 constructor families on both the Server (`Server/mse-router.js`) and the iPhone/Safari Userscript (`Extensions/src/mse-ui.js`, `mse.user.js`).
+
+This release resolves the long-standing limitation where multi-choice checkboxes in real Moodle instances (`qX:N_choice*`) were skipped, unlocks full drag-and-drop into text (`ddwtos`) with automated placeinput population and visual drop zone rendering, introduces sequential multi-control handling for mixed Cloze (`multianswer`) sub-questions in document order, eliminates prompt restrictions that blocked numbers and digits for numerical/calculated questions, and provides an exhaustive WebKit Playwright test suite guaranteeing DOM auto-fill correctness.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Key Features & Changes
+
+### A. Universal Question Parsing & Detection (`readQuestion`)
+* **Real Moodle Checkbox Recognition:** Expanded input detection regex from `/^q\d+:\d+_answer/` to `/^q\d+:\d+(_sub\d+)?_(answer|choice\d*)/`, successfully detecting real Moodle multi-choice checkboxes (`name="qX:N_choice0"`) and Cloze sub-question checkboxes.
+* **Document-Order Interactive Controls:** Re-architected control gathering to query interactive elements (`select, input[type=text][name], textarea[name], input.placeinput`) in exact DOM document order, ensuring multi-part answers match questions sequentially without field scrambling.
+* **`calculatedmulti` Reclassification:** Corrected `TYPE_INFO.calculatedmulti` kind to `'choice'` (previously incorrectly designated as `'text'`).
+* **`ddwtos` Parsing:** Added full extractor for draggable choices (`.draggrouphomes .draghome`) and hidden place inputs (`input.placeinput`), identifying choice index keys and target slot numbers.
+
+### B. Intelligent Auto-Filling (`applyAnswer`)
+* **Sequential Multi-Control Auto-Fill:** Implemented mixed-control sequencing for Cloze (`multianswer`), Matching (`match`), and Gapselect questions. If a question contains combinations of text inputs and select dropdowns, all slots are validated against prospective answers and applied in sequential order with proper `change` and `input` events.
+* **Drag-and-Drop Into Text (`ddwtos`):** Unlocked `ddwtos` in `TYPE_INFO` and removed it from `UNSUPPORTED`. Answers matching drag items are mapped to choice indices, populated into hidden `input.placeinput` elements, and rendered visually into `.drop` slots with clean placed styles.
+* **Real Moodle Checkboxes:** Multi-choice checkbox questions now correctly toggle multiple selections simultaneously and uncheck unselected options.
+* **Robust Single & Fallback Handling:** Single text inputs (`numerical`, `shortanswer`, `calculated`, `coderunner`) and single radio choices execute reliably with event dispatching.
+
+### C. Server & Agent Solver Prompts (`Server/mse-router.js` & `mse-server.js`)
+* **Digit Ban Lifted for Numeric & Calculated Questions:** Removed the blanket rule prohibiting digits and numbers in agent prompts. Numerical (`numerical`) and calculated (`calculated`, `calculatedsimple`, `calculatedmulti`) questions now instruct the LLM to provide exact numbers or decimals (e.g. 42 or 3.14).
+* **Universal Option Matching (`matchOption`):** Robust parser resolves options matching exact text, punctuation-normalized text (stripping trailing periods/colons), letter prefixes (`A.`, `A)`, `(A)` in Latin and Cyrillic `а-я`), numeric prefixes (`1.`, `1)`), bare index/letter fallbacks, and substring prefixes.
+* **Structured Multi-Field Prompting (`fields`):** For multianswer and mixed Cloze questions, sends a structured layout of each input in sequential DOM order, allowing the LLM to answer each slot accurately.
+* **Dedicated DDWTOS Prompting & Validation:** Added specialized prompts for drag-into-text questions with `N` blanks, instructing the agent to return choices in order separated by `|`. The router validates that every slot corresponds to an available draggable option.
+* **Free Text & Code Support:** Short answer and free-form fields now allow arbitrary text without requiring options matching.
+
+### D. Quality Assurance & WebKit Verification
+* **Exhaustive WebKit Test Suite:** Added `tests/question_types_real.test.js`, `tests/cloze_multianswer.test.js`, and `tests/ddwtos_real.test.js` running in Apple WebKit under Playwright to verify DOM interaction, event firing, and value propagation against real Moodle HTML.
+* **Rich Editor & Dynamic DOM Support:** Verified support for standard inputs, Moodle Atto editors, TinyMCE, `contenteditable` divs, and CodeRunner Ace editors.
+* **Comprehensive Test Pass:** All 23 router/gateway unit tests, 13 full end-to-end WebKit Playwright scenarios (`tests/mse.test.js`), 5 python bot tests, and all specialized type tests pass cleanly.
+* **Zero-Fingerprint Strict Audit:** Verified via `python3 scripts/audit.py --strict` with 0 hits across all files.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Layer 1 Support Matrix
+
+| Question Type | Category | Status in 2.12.0 | Form Field Mechanics |
+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `multichoice` (radio) | Choice | Supported | `<input type="radio" name="qX:N_answer">` |
+| `multichoice` (checkbox) | Choice | Supported | `<input type="checkbox" name="qX:N_choice\d+">` |
+| `multichoiceset` | Choice | Supported | `<input type="checkbox" name="qX:N_choice\d+">` |
+| `truefalse` | Choice | Supported | `<input type="radio" name="qX:N_answer">` |
+| `shortanswer` | Text | Supported | `<input type="text" name="qX:N_answer">` |
+| `numerical` | Text/Number | Supported | `<input type="text" name="qX:N_answer">` (digits allowed) |
+| `calculated` | Text/Number | Supported | `<input type="text" name="qX:N_answer">` (digits allowed) |
+| `calculatedsimple` | Text/Number | Supported | `<input type="text" name="qX:N_answer">` (digits allowed) |
+| `calculatedmulti` | Choice | Supported | `<input type="radio" / "checkbox">` |
+| `match` / `matching` | Select | Supported | Multiple `<select name="qX:N_sub\d+">` |
+| `gapselect` | Select | Supported | Multiple `<select name="qX:N_p\d+">` |
+| `multianswer` (Cloze) | Mixed | Supported | Sequential document-order `<select>`, `<input type="text">` |
+| `gapfill` | Text | Supported | Multiple `<input type="text" name="qX:N_p\d+">` |
+| `coderunner` | Text/Code | Supported | `<textarea name="qX:N_answer">` |
+| `ddwtos` | Drag/Drop | Supported | Hidden `input.placeinput` + `.draggrouphomes .draghome` |
+| `ddimageortext` | Visual Image | Described | Visual image drag (requires visual coordinate detection) |
+| `ddmarker` | Visual Image | Described | Visual canvas coordinates (requires image dropzone mapping) |
+| `essay` | Longform | Described | Manual submission / review required |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Verification Evidence
+
+1. `SS_BROWSER=webkit node --test tests/question_types_real.test.js`: PASS
+2. `SS_BROWSER=webkit node --test tests/cloze_multianswer.test.js`: PASS
+3. `SS_BROWSER=webkit node --test tests/ddwtos_real.test.js`: PASS
+4. `node --test tests/agent_types.test.js`: PASS
+5. `npm test`: PASS (23/23 tests)
+6. `npm run test:ext`: PASS (13/13 tests)
+7. `python3 tests/bot_selftest.py`: PASS (14 screens, 30 callbacks)
+8. `python3 scripts/audit.py --strict`: PASS (0 hits)
